    {
      "id": "1020627",
      "title": "Building an MCP Server for a React Component",
      "description": "Model Context Protocol, or MCP, is an emergent open-source standard, proposed by Anthropic, that is designed to provide a secure, standardized, and simple way to give AI systems the context they need. As this is a new standard, lots of things are still being defined. In this talk, we'll peel back the layers on MCP and leave you with everything you need to start building your own MCP server based on our own learnings at AG Grid.",
      "startsAt": "2025-10-07T22:40:00Z",
      "endsAt": "2025-10-07T22:50:00Z",
      "room": "Casablanca Ballroom ",
      "tags": [],
      "isServiceSession": false,
      "speakerIds": [
        "3a9bc435-1f20-4c8e-b5c7-aaa96a27e28f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1020628",
      "title": "Why React Native apps make all the money",
      "description": "React Native apps make more money than native and other cross-platform apps. This talk explains why, and shows how easy it is to add monetization to a React Native app.\r\n",
